<KnowledgeLayout title="Developer API Reference | TokenCalculator.dev Docs" description="Reference for the free TokenCalculator HTTP API: token counts, model usage, extracted file content, image geometry, costs, context, batch requests, comparisons, limits, and local SDK." heading="Developer API reference" eyebrow="HTTP API · v1" datePublished="2026-08-28" dateModified="2026-08-28" section="Developer API" keywords={['token counting API','LLM API cost estimator','tokenizer API','model comparison API','local token SDK']} type="TechArticle" {toc}>
  <p class="knowledge-lead">The TokenCalculator Developer API exposes the same normalized model catalog and measurement mechanics as the web application. Use the HTTP API for non-sensitive remote integrations and the npm SDK when prompts, code, or extracted files must remain inside your environment.</p>
  <div class="technical-callout"><span>Base URL</span><code>https://tokencalculator.dev/api/v1</code><span>Machine contract</span><code>https://tokencalculator.dev/openapi.json</code></div>
  <h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart</h2><p>No API key is required for the initial public v1 service.</p>
  <pre><code>{`curl https://tokencalculator.dev/api/v1/count \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
    "input": { "text": "Explain retrieval-augmented generation." },
    "output_tokens": 500
  }'`}</code></pre>
  <h2 id="request">Request schema</h2><p>A measurement accepts multiple content classes. TokenCalculator counts each part separately and returns an optional per-part breakdown.</p>
  <ul><li><code>model</code> — a model ID from <code>GET /models</code>.</li><li><code>input.text</code> — one raw prompt or text string.</li><li><code>input.messages[]</code> — role, optional name, and content. Raw content is measured; provider-added message framing is not inferred.</li><li><code>input.files[]</code> — a filename, optional media type, and already-extracted text or source code. Binary files are not accepted.</li><li><code>input.images[]</code> — pixel width, height, and low/high detail for provider-published vision formulas.</li><li><code>output_tokens</code> and <code>cached_input_tokens</code> — workload assumptions used by cost and context calculations.</li><li><code>options.include</code> — any of <code>usage</code>, <code>breakdown</code>, <code>cost</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>method</code>, and <code>pricing</code>.</li><li><code>metadata</code> — arbitrary caller data echoed unchanged for correlation.</li></ul>
  <h2 id="endpoints">Endpoints</h2><div class="table-shell overflow-x-auto"><table class="seo-table"><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/models</code></td><td>Model IDs, tokenizers, context, vision support, and verified pricing.</td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/count</code></td><td>One multimodal measurement.</td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/batch</code></td><td>Up to 25 independent measurements in input order.</td></tr><tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/compare</code></td><td>One input measured across up to ten models.</td></tr><tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/health</code></td><td>Availability and API version.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <h2 id="response">Response contract</h2><p>A full response can include:</p><ul><li><strong>usage:</strong> input, text, image, cached input, expected output, and total tokens.</li><li><strong>breakdown:</strong> token result, accuracy classification, and algorithm for every input part.</li><li><strong>cost:</strong> USD input, cache-read, output, and total projections.</li><li><strong>context:</strong> selected model window, maximum output, used and remaining capacity, ratio, and overflow state.</li><li><strong>method:</strong> exact/projected status, calculation algorithms, and explicit limitations.</li><li><strong>pricing:</strong> applied tier, unit rates, verification date, and primary source URL.</li></ul><p>Every successful response includes <code>X-Request-Id</code> and <code>X-API-Version</code> headers. Supply your own <code>X-Request-Id</code> (up to 96 characters) when you need correlation across systems.</p>
  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy, retention, and service limits</h2><p><strong>The public HTTP API is not browser-local.</strong> It receives payload content at the TokenCalculator.dev Cloudflare Worker. The application does not intentionally write request bodies to a database, object store, queue, or analytics dataset. Cloudflare may process infrastructure and security metadata under its platform controls.</p><p>Do not submit credentials, regulated data, confidential prompts, or proprietary source repositories. Use the local SDK or browser tool for that material.</p><ul><li>60 requests per minute, per route, connecting IP, and Cloudflare edge location.</li><li>256 KiB maximum JSON request body.</li><li>200 KiB combined UTF-8 text, message, and extracted-file content.</li><li>25 measurements per batch and 10 models per comparison.</li><li>No uptime SLA for the free public service.</li></ul>
  <h2 id="errors">Errors</h2><p>Errors use <code>application/problem+json</code> and the RFC 9457 fields <code>type</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>detail</code>, and <code>instance</code>. Expect 400 for invalid JSON or fields, 413 for body size, 415 for media type, 422 for range constraints, and 429 for rate limiting.</p>
  <h2 id="local-sdk">Local npm SDK</h2><p>Install the public package when request content must not cross the TokenCalculator.dev API boundary:</p><pre><code>{`npm install @jay0073/tokencalculator-core

import { measureModel, compareModels } from '@jay0073/tokencalculator-core';

const result = await measureModel({
  text: privatePrompt,
  image: { width: 1920, height: 1080, detail: 'high' },
  outputTokens: 500,
}, 'gpt-5.6-terra');`}</code></pre><p>The SDK currently accepts raw/extracted text and one image measurement per call. Browser-side PDF and DOCX extraction remains part of the web application; pass its extracted content to the SDK if you are building your own private ingestion pipeline.</p>
  <div class="source-ledger"><h2>Standards and runtime references</h2><ul><li><a href="https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.2.html">OpenAPI Specification 3.1.2</a></li><li><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457.html">RFC 9457: Problem Details for HTTP APIs</a></li><li><a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/routing/worker-script/">Cloudflare Workers static assets and API routing</a></li><li><a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/rate-limit/">Cloudflare Workers Rate Limiting binding</a></li></ul></div>
